A||||16||firstfiero||over heating problem...need opinion please..||||9||
Z||000000||firstfiero||04-06-2001||10:07 PM||||    About 4 weeks ago while ideling waiting for someone me fiero (86se) starting overheating. I shut her down until the person came out. When I pulled out of the gas station it was still rising till I gunned then it started going down in a hurry. <BR>    Today I was sitting in alot of traffic and what do you know but my heat light pops on and it s red lineing. Tonight on the way home from work...even hee hawing around with the kids on the circuit...my car was fine. <BR>    By the way I don't need anti freeze...checked that. I think its just a thermostat sticking. At least I hope so  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">..that's an  easy cheap thing. My question is where the hell is it? front or back.anything I should know that's odd for a fiero and if you agree with my oppinion of what's wrong would be helpful. Thanks<P>------------------<BR>NO MR. RICER STICKERS DON'T MAKE YOU FASTER!!<BR> Todd<BR>    86se||||reg||9
Z||000001||FieroJoe||04-06-2001||10:45 PM||||The thermostat is located on a filler neck on the left side of the head.  There usually is also a sensor in the neck too.  It has a silver cap on it, similar to a radiator cap.<P>If that is all that is causing your problems, then you have yourself a real cheap fix.<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||fyerstarter||04-06-2001||10:54 PM||||Sounds to me like you got a bad fan switch since it's happening in traffic and when you are standing still and not when you are going fast. Get the car up to normal operatig temperature and then pop your hood and see if the fan is coming on. If not then a new fan switch is like 10 bucks from the local AutoParts store.||||reg||1
Z||000003||firstfiero||04-06-2001||11:08 PM||||       Already checked the fan...thats working perfectly. The only other thing it could be is the water pump...But you can usually hear that going bad. So the thermostat is only a 10 dollar part...so I guess I'll try that. <P>------------------<BR>Hey Mr. Ricer come over here and tell me how your stickers make you faster.....<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/headshot.gif"> <BR>Todd <BR>  86se||||reg||4
Z||000004||theogre||04-06-2001||11:22 PM||||radiator blockage would also do this.... something blocking air flow or water flow or both... most likely water flow.||||reg||1
