Z||000009||firstfiero||04-07-2001||10:47 AM||||      Thanks for the help guys. Where does your temp. guage usually hang. Mine stays at about the quarter mark and a little bit higher if I'm sitting in traffic. Thanks<P>------------------<BR>Hey Mr. Ricer come over here and tell me how your stickers make you faster.....<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/headshot.gif"> <BR>Todd <BR>  86se||||reg||14
Z||000010||theogre||04-07-2001||12:32 PM||||since fixing the heater core last year mine sits on the first blank mark. It stays there unless I'm idled for a very long time. It creeps up just a hair in slow traffic.<P><BR>This is with the fan off and no hood mods or anything like that.||||reg||1
Z||000011||firstfiero||04-07-2001||03:09 PM||||That sounds right then...Maybe it was just an air buble.<P>------------------<BR>Hey Mr. Ricer come over here and tell me how your stickers make you faster.....<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/headshot.gif"> <BR>Todd <BR>  86se||||reg||14
Z||000012||Windsor62||04-07-2001||07:03 PM||||... just another thing to check... the terminal block in the engine compatment (right side, by the battery)... check to make sure it's secure... give it  "wiggle" and snug the bolt holding it in place (1/4")<BR>...<P>Just rebuilt my buddy's 2.8, and there was a bad connection when we hooked it back up... kept the fan from coming on & made it overheat....   tightened this connector and it's fine now...<P>Happy Fiero'ing<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000013||84Bill||04-07-2001||08:41 PM||||--------------------------------------<BR>Mine usually goes up to the first tick and hangs there. it only goes up just a smidge in trafficand on hot days in traffic it will go past the half mark until the fan kicks on.<P>BTW Do you hear any noises when your car gets hot? Usually you can hear a rumbel or muffeld bang from the car when its overheated. This is the boiling coolant (air) in the coolant lines. <P>KEEP THE OVERFLOW TANK WET! if its dry (cool engine) you got air in the system. NO DOUBT<P>||||reg||1
Z||000014||c m west||04-07-2001||08:43 PM||||crushed cooland tubes - cause - unexperienced mechanic throwing you car on a lift thinking the coolant transfer tubes are a lift point. reshape or rebend if possible, replace with radiator hose if neccassary.<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
